(project pricklypear-filmstrip
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: FILMSTRIP — the habitat shell. Two infinite horizontal strips stacked iTunes-style: the top strip is a Miller-column cascade (structural menus, not popups), the bottom strip is the niri-style row of content panes. Panes are ordinary routes in partial mode — they don't know they're windowed. Workspace state is a per-user row; the desktop persists in the same object store as the todos it displays.")
 (status implemented)
 (* agent note (|2026-09 DESIGN SESSION (with pads.borg): the user's sketch (waybar + three small top panels + one large content area, \"kind of how iTunes is laid out\") plus \"two separate infinite horizontal panes\" crystallized the model. Prior art named in-session: iTunes column browser / Finder column view / ranger / Smalltalk browser for the top (Miller-column cascade); niri (and not-quite acme) for the bottom. The point that made it click: the cascade is STATE, not styling — which is why the filmstrip idea never modalized in CSS. Filmstrip is the FIRST consumer of pads vocabulary but is itself buildable stringly as a product; pads migration makes it provable. Dialog/overlay needs come from pads/layers-modality; filmstrip keeps floats for genuinely transient things only — navigation is structural.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04 MAKE (filmstrip v1, branch filmstrip-v1): shell shipped stringly per the handoff plan (docs/plans/filmstrip-v1.md). Dialect notes for the next agent: let* is a SINGLE-BODY macro — multi-step handlers wrap their tail in (seq ...); cons builds VPair chains which count rejects (length accepts both). browse lives as <pkg>/browse defs inside libs/filmstrip until promotion into todo/notes/calendar. Routes are exact-match, so /filmstrip/width/<id> became /filmstrip/<action> routes with id/dir/d/t params — same semantics, different spelling than this chapter's prose. Smoke: scripts/smoke_filmstrip.py (11 checks incl. zero-JS + round-trip).|) *)
 (convention ocaml-dune)

 (section filmstrip-shell
  (doc "The default habitat view. Screen model: a column of two rows —
      the cascade strip (short, iTunes browser proportions) over the
      content strip (grow). Both scroll horizontally and independently;
      both are ordinary pad rows with (scroll . x) once pads exists.
      Panes do not know they are windowed: a pane is any route
      dispatched in partial mode (HX-Request on — the route gate's
      existing fragment path, the hyper/visit trick productized). All
      htmx inside a pane works unchanged, targeting its own fragment.")

  (subsection workspace-model
   (doc "Per-user workspace row: two sequences plus focus. cascade = an
       ordered crumb path; content = an ordered list of pane records
       {id route width}; focus = (strip . index). Open/close/focus/
       width-preset are row mutations rendered back as swaps — the
       strip follows niri's set-column-width presets (third / half /
       full), never free pixel widths. Sessions persist: close the
       laptop, the strip is where you left it, because the row is
       Postgres like everything else grown in the garden.")
   (details
    (doc (|
         ROW SHAPE (target):
           (ws (user)
             (cascade (list \"packages\" \"todo\" \"today\"))
             (content (list (pane todo/today 'half)
                            (pane notes/inbox 'third)))
             (focus (cons 'content 0)))
         EPHEMERAL CORNER (pads/layers-modality rule applied): scroll
         position, hovered pane, live-drag in progress — transient,
         keyed by pane id, patched around on sync; never rendered from.
    |))
   )
   (implements libs/filmstrip/lib.pp scripts/smoke_filmstrip.py)
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection cascade-protocol
   (doc "The top strip is a Miller-column cascade: column N's selection
       determines column N+1; the deepest selection acts on the content
       strip. One function per package makes it filmstrip-native:
       (pkg/browse path) -> (columns . leaf?). Clicking an entry at
       depth d truncates the path to d, appends the choice, swaps the
       tail columns. Leaf action opens-or-focuses a content pane.
       Menus as STRUCTURE, not popups — plan 9's menus-are-text moved
       from overlay into chrome; the float band survives only for
       genuinely transient things (confirmations, plumbing menus,
       notifications).")
   (details
    (doc (|
         BROWSE IS THE WHOLE TRICK. Every package already has the
         shape, it just renders it wrong today:
           notes     outline headings walk down
           calendar  year -> month -> day
           bible     book -> chapter -> verse (dabar/strongs adjacent)
           contacts  group -> person
           todo      list -> item
         DECISION RECORDED: cascade is GLOBAL v1 — one crumb path for
         the shell, iTunes-style. Per-pane cascades (each content pane
         carrying its own crumb path, workspace = N uniform cascade+
         content columns) is the elegant unification but doubles the
         state surface; revisit after v1 is dogfooded. NOTIFICATIONS:
         transient cards in the cascade strip (waybar's \"pi finished\"
         earns a home), promotable into content panes or dismissed —
         filmstrip gives notifications a place to LIVE that isn't a
         popup.
    |))
   )
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection pane-protocol
   (doc "A pane = route dispatched in-process with HX-Request on, the
       route gate's existing fragment path. Zero-JS hotkeys: htmx key
       filters on the shell body (keydown[altKey&&key=='ArrowLeft'] and
       kin) POST focus/width/open to filmstrip routes; the server owns
       which pane wears .focused and answers with OOB class swaps.
       Optional JS is quarantined to ONE static file and buys only
       scroll-into-view smoothness and horizontal wheel mapping —
       nothing semantic. Twin-pane mode is a first-class pane kind for
       the pads migration: one column showing [old string render |
       pads-lowered render | soup/diff badge] — drift as something you
       LOOK at, pads/drift-proofing made interactive.")
   (details
    (doc (|
         NO NEW SUBSTRATE inventory (why this is a product, not a
         research project): route/lookup + route/dispatch with the
         header seam already exist; the route gate already serves
         partial mode; css/sheet + theme/ extend to ~50 lines of strip
         CSS; the workspace row is data_rows; the only optional
         non-Nopales artifact is the quarantined scroll.js. Nothing in
         image/ moves for v1.
    |))
   )
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection shell-events
   (doc "Open: launcher picks a route, POST /filmstrip/open, server
       appends the pane record and dispatches the route — fragment goes
       beforeend into the strip. Close/width/focus likewise: row
       mutation, then minimal OOB swaps (this is the ops-contract of
       pads worn by the web backend before pads exists — the shell is
       the ops pilot). Dialogs and menus follow pads/layers-modality:
       a #layers sibling of the strips takes float/scrim nodes; modal
       = router scope while the node lives.")
   (verify
    (smoke "open todo -> strip gains pane with todo partial; interactions inside pane swap in-place")
    (smoke "alt+arrows move .focused between panes with no JS")
    (smoke "workspace row round-trip: reload restores strip order/widths/focus")
    (smoke "cascade: packages -> todo -> today opens the today pane; truncation re-walks"))
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection window-controlbox-v2
   (doc "V2 shell model (glochid-led, habitat-shared). Two primitives, following acme: WINDOW = tag + body (tag row of words over a dispatched route fragment; the filmstrip pane head already IS a tag), CONTROLBOX = one labeled row of words where each word is a mutation POST (rail rows, pane heads, shelf rows are all control boxes). Everything renders from DECLARED STATE, never estimate geometry in code: panes gain region (rail | main), desktop (int), state (live | shelved); the workspace row grows a desktop int. The shell is two scroll-strips — a RAIL strip (vertical on wide-short screens, top-rotatable by 3 CSS rules; modes are rail panes: apps/files/windows/shelf, for PICKING not reading) over a MAIN strip (the niri horizontal strip third/half/full, unconditional) — same mutations on both. VIRTUAL DESKTOPS are class flips: one sentinel carries the current desktop, a generated :has() set display:nones the rest; zero JS. Shelf is the DEFAULT close (DOM survives via hx-preserve; shelf rows carry destroy; destroy is the OOB delete that exists today). NAV DISCIPLINE is part of the vocabulary: app-link = open-or-focus POST for cross-app nav; pane-local links target closest .fs-body; plain <a> is shell-level only (a pane escaping the shell — plain <a> inside a fragment — is a BUG CLASS, fixed by app-link). Focus always heals so a focused main pane exists while panes do. make harness: seeded fake workspace on a scratch instance, CDP screenshots with measured geometry per mutation; live hosts touched last.")
   (* agent note (|2026-09-13 DESIGN SESSION (glochid rail work): the col axis grew the left rail (shell narrows to ~20rem; cascade stacks as a vertical app menu; presets re-read as rail heights — landed), then the focused pane was LIFTED into the main window via position:fixed with rail rows heads-only (landed; .chatpage height:100% fix landed with it). Session then RENAMED the target: main = niri strip (option B, not master-stack), sidebar = own scroll strip, desktops like hyprland via CSS hiding, close defaults to shelf, no JS drag — never. Inspiration named: acme tag lines = control boxes; gui-better-than-tui via TWO simple primitives instead of a renderer. Hidden-DOM cost confirmed negligible; live-updating shelved DOM is the only budget (later: server pauses streams to shelved panes). What landed pre-v2 stays in agent.borg filmstrip-shell; THIS stanza owns the forward model.|) *)
   (* agent note (|2026-09-14 UI REVIEW CYCLE CLOSED (dogfood + agent review, docs/reviews/glochid-shell-review-2026-09-14.md): the review CONFIRMED this stanza's model but caught three behavior gaps the geometry probes PASSED — (a) open-or-focus didn't know state: clicking a shelved app's cascade name moved .focused onto a display:none pane and BLANKED the main window; FIXED acme-get style (naming a hidden window re-shows it — open-apply unshelves on route hit) in 22906c9; (b) open/cascade mutations never refreshed the windows rail, so #fs-winbox went stale; FIXED same commit (shelf/winbox OOB hooks now answered on every open win); (c) the plain-<a> bug class was still live on every fragment surface (/code rows, chat h1 'agent' + resumed line, sessions resume/view, settings h1) — /code rows are pane-local links now (hx-target closest .fs-body, the tree walk stays INSIDE the pane), redirect-actions got fragment twins (POST /filmstrip/new, /filmstrip/resume; 2db1008), settings fragment h1 de-anchored (9a7bd3b via probe I5). The launcher advertised /todos on glochid (host vocab leak): placeholder + no-route message now derive from filmstrip/ hints themselves (hint-routes over the host's apps — glochid ALSO redefines filmstrip/apps now, which the host-variation note already named as allowed). The open-apply no-desktop gap (REPORT of docs/plans/window-controlbox-v2.md) is CLOSED via the filmstrip/pane-stamp host hook: fresh panes stamp the operator's current desktop. NEW HARNESS: scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs asserts the invariants semantically (I1 visible-focused-always · I2 shelved-click unshelves · I3 winbox freshness · I4 launcher honesty · I5 pane-local anchors · I6 in-pane tree walk · I7 current-desktop stamp) — ALL GREEN, lisp/common runtest green, chat smoke green.|) *)
   (implements scripts/probe_shell_wm.mjs scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs)
   (verify
    (smoke "desktop flip: sentinel class change toggles which panes render; others display:none but keep live DOM")
    (smoke "shelve: close moves pane to the shelf rail pane with DOM intact; restore returns it to its desktop+position")
    (smoke "app-link inside a pane open-or-focuses the target route; a plain <a> inside a fragment never escapes the shell")
    (smoke "geometry probe: seeded 8-pane 3-desktop workspace renders from state classes only (no inline styles)")
    (smoke "semantic probe (scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs): I1 visible-focused-always · I2 shelved-click unshelves (no 0x0 focused pane) · I3 winbox freshness · I4 launcher names only real host routes · I5 every fragment anchor pane-local · I6 /code dir walk inside the pane · I7 fresh panes stamp the current desktop — ALL GREEN")
    (smoke "open-or-focus on a shelved route UNSHELVES it (acme Get); launcher placeholder + no-route message list only routes the host has"))
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection window-controlbox-v3
   (doc "V3 shell model: REGION SHIPS. window-controlbox-v2 declared panes gain region (rail | main) — the implementation never read it, so the rail is heads-only and exactly ONE body is ever on stage; the operator cannot hold two reading views at once (file tree + chat — the 2026-09-14 review's biggest ask + its design findings 1-3: dead rail middle, 16rem-capped cascade that cannot grow into the space it owns). V3 implements region as a pane-head PIN verb. region=rail panes render their LIVE BODY inside the rail (between the cascade and the controlboxes — filling the dead middle); region=main panes keep the v2 model (strip + one lifted focused pane, unchanged). RAIL PANES ARE DESKTOP-GLOBAL (dock semantics: one sidebar visible across desktop flips — no per-desktop duplication of a file tree). At most one lifted main pane exists at a time; focusing a rail pane highlights it WITHOUT lifting; open-or-focus of a pinned route highlights the rail pane in place instead of stealing the main window (and must never heal-focus onto a shelved pane — the I2 invariant holds in both regions). The FILE TREE graduates from a cascade walk to a pinned /code pane: the cascade keeps only PICKING (column 0 apps), the rail pane is the READING view at full rail height. Pane records carry region; all geometry stays in glochid/base-css as classes + :has — zero JS, zero inline styles, same discipline as v2. Make harness: scratch instance + CDP with scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs (batch B) as the GATE — semantic invariants first, geometry second; live hosts last.")
   (verify
    (smoke "pin /code -> its body renders in the rail at a real height while /chat stays lifted in the main window; zero inline styles introduced")
    (smoke "rail pin survives desktop flips (dock semantics); unpin returns the pane to the strip at its old position")
    (smoke "open-or-focus on a pinned route highlights the rail pane in place (no lift, no 0x0 focused pane, I1/I2 hold)")
    (smoke "probe_shell_sem.mjs ALL GREEN after every mutation (invariants are the gate; extend it with region invariants)")
    (smoke "shelving a rail-region pane shelves it like any pane (shelf row; restore restores region)")
    (smoke "a pinned files view fills available rail height — the cascade 16rem cap no longer bounds it")
    (smoke "workspace round-trip: region persists through save-all and reload")
   )
   (* agent note (|2026-09-14 MAKE (window-controlbox-v3) DONE via the plan loop (docs/plans/window-controlbox-v3.md REPORT, commits 476f4db..55619a5 + ca7a9d8): region is a first-class pane state (records + data-region + native-scene); POST /filmstrip/pin flips it with the width-grammar OOBs; pin words in pane-head + win-row; rail-region panes render their LIVE BODY in the rail at flex rail-share (the cascade 16rem cap never touches them), desktop-GLOBAL (exempt from the desk :has hiding — dock semantics); focus/open/cascade never lift a rail pane (in-place live-DOM ring; a focused rail pane satisfies the visible-focus invariant when no main pane is live); healing (render heal-focus AND a new lib close-heal — the loop's probe caught v2's first-live-index healing onto HIDDEN 0x0 main panes when a pinned pane was closed on a foreign desktop) prefers main-on-current-desk, then dock-visible rail panes, never shelved. /code walks pane-locally at rail height. probe_shell_sem.mjs extended to the v3 block: 82 assertions ALL GREEN (default + final passes); geometry probe matches the v2 baseline with pinned bands as flex shares; chat smoke green; lisp/common runtest green; borge drift 0. Zero inline styles. Weak points deferred: rail focus ring is live-DOM state (server can re-derive on reload); shelved-DOM stream pause still open budget.|) *)
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection rail-trees-v4
   (doc "V4 rail model: ONE TREE GRAMMAR. The rail's inventory stops being N bespoke renderers and becomes N TREES over one control — mode tabs switch between ROOTS, not widget types. A TREE IS A GEOMETRY RULE OVER CONTROLBOXES, NOT A THIRD PRIMITIVE: a tree row is an acme tag-line row — leading FOLD arrow (its own hitbox, never coalesced with the label), LABEL word (navigates / open-or-focus — safe, acme Get on hidden things), TRAILING VERB words (mutation POSTs only: focus / shelve / destroy / pin). NO third interaction is ever added (no double-click, no context menus — words acme-execute, that is the whole grammar). A toolbar is a degenerate tree node (words, no children); 'every toolbar renders as a tree' is the unifier, and the shelf collapses into the window-control tree as a SUBTREE instead of its own face. HATEOAS NODES: every node carries its affordances as links; the app convention is a `/app/tree` route answering ONE LEVEL as a fragment — splice a nested <ul> into the open <details> (outline projection) or swap a replacement level into a drill container (drill-down projection; nested tree is Miller rotated 90°, SAME endpoint, template chosen by target, never a forked API). LAZY LEVELS ARE LOAD-BEARING: never render a whole tree server-side (the notes/doc/get 80s floor); expand fetches the next level, on first expand only. STATE LIVES IN THE DOM: folds are native <details>/<summary> — ZERO JS, ZERO server-side expansion state; mode flips, desktop flips, and shelving all preserve it for free (sentinel :has hiding + hx-preserve). Splice-inplace, NEVER re-render a level; the tree's head carries a `collapse-all` word (a mutation POST — grammar holds) as the DOM-growth escape hatch. TREES ARE DESKTOP-GLOBAL like any v3 rail panes: global roots (windows / files; glochid adds prims / packages) commute with app-contributed roots — a pinned rail pane contributes its tree as another rail MODE (chat -> contacts tree, calendar -> month-selector tree, todo -> list tree), and targeting-trees (nodes' verbs act on panes: window-control tree — requires panes to answer a route-derived node path) coexist with contents-trees (package -> prim -> function-doc leaves; describe made browsable). MOBILE EARNS THE PIVOT: fold IS the native small-screen nav gesture; responsive = DEPTH, not a new widget — past ~4 indent levels the drill-down projection takes over (level + breadcrumb back), and narrow viewports demote trailing verbs to an `actions` FOLD (verbs-as-children) while CSS :has hides the inline words; Miller columns died on phones, this doesn't. Make harness: scratch instance + probe_shell_sem.mjs batch C (tree invariants) as the gate; geometry probe after; live hosts last.")
   (* agent note (|2026-09-13 DESIGN SESSION (rail trees, glochid-led): the session started from 'Miller is dead on widescreen, sidebars win — what if we just got REALLY GOOD at rendering trees in the sidebar, every window its own nested tree control, generated via HATEOAS' and sharpened into: (a) nested outline vs drill-down are TWO PROJECTIONS of one HATEOAS endpoint (nested tree = Miller rotated, drill-down = Miller on phones); (b) expansion state was the genuinely-undesigned piece — resolved as NEVER THE SERVER'S PROBLEM: <details> DOM state survives every flip because rail modes/desktop flips are :has sentinel hides and shelf is hx-preserve — splice never swap, collapse-all word as the pressure valve; (c) the acme split named for the record (the filmstrip spec already quotes acme: tag lines = word-rows that execute): label = open (safe), trailing words = verbs (mutate), fold arrow = isolated leading hitbox — the FIRST interaction on the grammar is also the LAST, no double-click ever; (d) 'every toolbar is a tree' <-> 'every controlbox is a degenerate tree node' is the real unification claim, shelf-as-subtree is its first proof; (e) mobile worry answered IN GRAMMAR: verbs demote to children on narrow rails, drill-down caps indentation depth — responsive depth, no overflow-menu widget; (f) scope guard against 'everything becomes a tree': only STRUCTURE faces become trees (contacts, month selectors, prim catalogs) — stream faces (chat body, calendar month grid, todo list body) stay bodies; targeting vs contents tree distinction recorded in the stanza. Open seam for make: whether <app>/tree returns outline-vs-drill fragments by route PARAM or by hx-target of the request — stanza leaves it to the first implementer, both are conformant.|) *)
   (verify
    (smoke "the rail's N mode contents all render through ONE tree renderer (windows / files / host extras); mode tab flips swap visible root only — expansion state of every root survives the flip")
    (smoke "row grammar: fold arrow toggles without opening; label open-or-focuses (v2 acme-Get semantics — naming a shelved pane unshelves); every trailing verb POSTs and never navigates; no row has a third interaction")
    (smoke "lazy levels: first render of any root emits exactly ONE level via /app/tree?node=<path>; expanding a node fetches its level exactly once; re-folding never refetches; collapse-all restores the head state with one POST")
    (smoke "shelf a live rail tree -> restore it: expanded nodes and scroll position intact (hx-preserve); desktop flip leaves all rail trees DOM-live and hidden-state-clean")
    (smoke "a pinned rail pane contributes its tree as a rail mode (chat contacts tree visible beside windows and files roots); unpining the pane removes its mode; open-or-focus on a tree label highlights the rail pane in place without lifting (I1/I2 hold)")
    (smoke "narrow/rail-min geometry: indent caps visibly past level 4 and the drill projection serves deeper levels; trailing verbs collapse into the actions fold; probe measured — zero inline styles, glochid/base-css classes only")
    (smoke "window-control tree reflects DECLARED STATE: shelve a pane -> its row moves under the shelf subtree on OOB; desktop int annotates rows from the workspace record, never from DOM scraping")
    (smoke "probe_shell_sem.mjs batch C green (tree invariants alongside I1-I7 + v3 region assertions); downlevel surfaces (chat smoke, /code pane walk) still green"))
   (* agent note (|2026-09-13 MAKE (rail-trees-v4) DONE (docs/plans/rail-trees-v4.md): ONE renderer in the lib (node dicts with verbs as JSON strings -- dict-set* refuses non-string values), /filmstrip/tree + /tree/collapse routes, url-enc/dec (SUBSTRING takes START LEN, not END -- the per-char walk must slice 1/2-char windows), <details> + hx-trigger "toggle once" lazy levels (fetch exactly once, provable via performance entries); glochid hosts windows/code/prims roots, rail mode tabs + #fs-railmode sentinel (:has, like the desktops). TWO mid-make discoveries: (1) OOB-swapping the whole box div made htmx drop listeners for subsequently spliced levels (0 XHRs on verb clicks) -- the mutation refresh seam is now an hx-swap-oob="innerHTML" on the level-0 UL (fs-tree-<id>-root); the head never changes and expansion state above the mutated rows SURVIVES mutations (truer to the DOM-state rule than the first draft) -- expansion loss at mutations was the first draft's design hole, closed by the same move; (2) acme Get on a CROSS-DESKTOP shelved row re-showed the pane on its OLD desktop (0x0 focused pane, latent v2/v3 bug the tree's cross-desk rows made reachable) -- open-apply's unshelve branch now passes through pane-stamp like fresh panes. probe_shell_sem.mjs: batch C landed, whole probe ALL GREEN (104 assertions: I1-I8 + T0-T6); agent tests +22 incl rail-trees; agent surface smoke updated to the v4 close contract (shelve OOB + tree rows, not the pre-v2 pane delete); chat model <select> inline style -> .fs-modelsel class. Substring of the session also landed the in-flight bindings-browser work this stanza builds on (bind/* bridge prims + /bindings face + cascade crumb).|) *)
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection sidebar-main-dichotomy
   (doc "THE SHELL'S NAV MODEL, one rule: trees live in the SIDEBAR
       (the col-axis rail), interfaces live in the MAIN window. The
       cascade is an interface PICKER only — its column 0 entries are
       route LEAVES that open-or-focus a main-window pane; no host
       ships cascade walk entries (structure browsing is tree work,
       not menu work). The rail's inventory comes from rail-trees-v4,
       and the windows tree is the ONE rendering of the pane inventory
       — desktop rows (desktop 0..9) carry the switch verb, live pane
       rows carry focus / pin / width / close, shelved panes are
       restore / destroy rows under the shelf subtree — so a host
       renders NO sibling desktop switcher, pane-tag strip, or
       standalone shelf beside it: any second rendering of the pane
       inventory is a stale copy waiting to drift. In the col axis an
       unfocused main pane renders NOWHERE: a pane is visible as the
       lifted focused main pane, a pinned (region=rail) body, or a row
       of the windows tree. There is no route-text launcher — opening
       is PICKING (cascade or tree). The axis toggle is a word on the
       rail tabs row (its last entry). Filmstrip the framework keeps
       the walk-capable cascade and the launcher/open endpoint as
       primitives; the dichotomy is glochid's COMPOSITION of them —
       glochid's column 0 is all leaves, its shell has no launcher, no
       pane-tag strip, and no desktop controlbox.")
   (verify
    (smoke "cascade column 0 entries are all route leaves; each open-or-focuses a main-window pane")
    (smoke "the col rail renders no pane-tag strip, desktop switcher controlbox, or launcher; the windows tree is the pane inventory")
    (smoke "an unfocused main pane is absent from the col rail; focusing its tree row (or a shelf restore) lifts or shows it")
    (smoke "the axis toggle renders as a word on the rail tabs row and persists through reload"))
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection action-glyphs
   (doc "THE UI VOCABULARY IS GLYPHS, and the word is metadata. An
       action button renders a GLYPH; the verb WORD survives on it as
       title (a human tooltip), aria-label (the accessible name) and
       data-verb (the queryable identity). 'pin' / 'width' / 'close' /
       'focus' were implementation vocabulary leaking into the UI -- a
       user does not know what pinning MEANS, and a decision is not a
       word; the glyphs are the decision, the words are its
       documentation. This refines, and does not repeal, the
       rail-trees-v4 acme row grammar: the split (fold arrow =
       children, label = safe open-or-focus, trailing GLYPHS =
       mutation verbs) is unchanged -- only the verb's rendering
       changed from word to glyph, and the word moved to the tooltip
       and data attributes. GLYPHS ARE HOST VOCABULARY: the table
       filmstrip/act-glyphs (verb word -> glyph) lives in the LIB so
       the lib's own pane head has a default, and a host redefines
       that ONE value for another glyph set -- no renderer fork (same
       seam discipline as filmstrip/apps). A verb absent from the
       table renders its WORD: glyphs are an improvement over words,
       never a hard requirement, and a missing glyph must never render
       a blank button. ROW GRAMMAR (rails trees): fold arrow, label,
       then the glyphs. THE ACTIONS FOLD IS NARROW-ONLY -- it is the
       responsive demotion of those same glyphs (responsive = depth,
       not a new widget), a PLAIN ul child of the node's own
       <details>, with NO summary of its own and NO duplicate of the
       node: at rail width the glyphs are hidden in the row and the
       fold reveals them as children, past the breakpoint the fold is
       hidden and the glyphs are inline. Exactly ONE of the two is
       visible at any width; a nested 'actions' summary row that
       re-lists verbs already shown inline is the bug this rule
       prohibits (it also duplicated the parent's verbs at child
       depth). Pane head (filmstrip/pane-head): the same contract --
       pin/unpin, width and close are glyphs with the same tooltip /
       aria-label / data-verb trio, so the rail's rows and the lifted
       pane's header never disagree about vocabulary. rail mode tabs
       and collapse-all: the tab names are CONTENT labels (like the
       cascade's app names) and stay words; collapse-all is an action
       and is a glyph. Every action button carries data-verb so
       probes + tests select by identity, never by rendered glyph --
       the glyph is free to change.")
   (verify
    (smoke "every action button in the rail trees and the pane head renders a glyph and carries title, aria-label and data-verb (the word is metadata, never the label)")
    (smoke "a verb missing from filmstrip/act-glyphs renders its word -- never an empty button; redefining the table re-labels every surface at once")
    (smoke "at rail width the row shows glyphs and the actions fold is hidden; past the breakpoint the glyphs are hidden and the fold reveals them -- never both, never neither")
    (smoke "no tree row renders a nested actions summary or a second verb list beside the inline glyphs (the duplication regression)")
    (smoke "probe_shell_sem.mjs T7 green: glyph + data-verb + aria-label + tooltip on every action button, no visible duplicate fold at rail width"))
